WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.450
Semicolons and Colons

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:06.684
Semicolon = period. Colon = here’s what I mean.

00:00:07.884 --> 00:00:08.975
How to spot it

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.956
Semicolons and colons in the choices

00:00:12.506 --> 00:00:14.393
A blank between two parts

00:00:14.943 --> 00:00:18.922
It’s testing: the exact job of each punctuation mark

00:00:20.122 --> 00:00:20.888
The method

00:00:21.288 --> 00:00:24.495
Step 1: Semicolon? Test both sides

00:00:24.775 --> 00:00:26.611
Each must be a full sentence.

00:00:27.161 --> 00:00:30.147
Step 2: Colon? Test the left side

00:00:30.427 --> 00:00:32.164
It must be a full sentence.

00:00:32.714 --> 00:00:35.717
Step 3: Does the right side explain?

00:00:35.997 --> 00:00:39.093
A list, example or explanation fits a colon.

00:00:39.643 --> 00:00:42.616
Step 4: Never after a verb

00:00:42.896 --> 00:00:45.492
“The ingredients are:” is wrong.

00:00:46.042 --> 00:00:47.137
In a few words

00:00:47.287 --> 00:00:51.415
Semicolon: both sides. Colon: left side.

00:00:52.615 --> 00:00:53.397
The rules

00:00:53.797 --> 00:00:55.538
Semicolon = period

00:00:55.818 --> 00:00:59.331
Wrong: The lab was quiet; because everyone left.

00:00:59.611 --> 00:01:03.046
Right: The lab was quiet; everyone had left.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.688
Colon needs a full sentence first

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:09.493
Wrong: The ingredients are: flour and eggs.

00:01:09.773 --> 00:01:12.226
Right: She had one goal: winning.

00:01:12.776 --> 00:01:15.683
After a colon: explain, list, show

00:01:15.963 --> 00:01:19.987
Right: The cause was clear: the battery overheated.

00:01:20.537 --> 00:01:23.196
Semicolons split lists that have commas

00:01:23.476 --> 00:01:28.254
Right: Nairobi, Kenya; Lima, Peru; and Hanoi, Vietnam

00:01:29.454 --> 00:01:30.515
Let’s try one

00:01:30.915 --> 00:01:35.809
The ship’s log revealed the cause of the delay ______ a storm had forced the crew to shelter in a

00:01:35.809 --> 00:01:37.415
harbor for six days.

00:01:38.065 --> 00:01:43.866
Left side: the ship’s log revealed the cause of the delay. That’s a full sentence.

00:01:44.416 --> 00:01:46.894
The right side explains what the cause was.

00:01:47.444 --> 00:01:51.207
A comma makes a splice. Nothing makes a run-on.

00:01:51.207 --> 00:01:55.894
And loses the link. A colon introduces the explanation.

00:01:55.894 --> 00:01:56.777
Choice B.

00:01:57.977 --> 00:01:59.046
Common traps

00:01:59.446 --> 00:02:00.887
Colon after a verb

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:05.250
“includes:” or “are:” leaves the left side incomplete.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.847
Semicolon before a fragment

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:10.159
Both sides must stand alone.

00:02:11.359 --> 00:02:13.208
Semicolons and Colons

00:02:13.488 --> 00:02:17.616
Semicolon: both sides. Colon: left side.

00:02:18.166 --> 00:02:18.746
Spot it

00:02:18.946 --> 00:02:21.527
Semicolons and colons in the choices

00:02:22.077 --> 00:02:22.784
Steps

00:02:22.984 --> 00:02:26.537
1. Semicolon: both sides full sentences

00:02:26.817 --> 00:02:29.828
2. Colon: left side a full sentence

00:02:30.108 --> 00:02:33.641
3. Right side explains or lists? → colon

00:02:33.921 --> 00:02:36.306
4. Never a colon right after a verb

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:37.581
Remember

00:02:37.781 --> 00:02:39.522
Semicolon = period

00:02:39.802 --> 00:02:42.097
Colon needs a full sentence before it

00:02:42.377 --> 00:02:45.453
After a colon: explanation, list, example

00:02:45.733 --> 00:02:48.772
Semicolons split list items that have commas

00:02:49.322 --> 00:02:49.763
Trap

00:02:49.963 --> 00:02:52.257
Colon after a verb or “such as”

00:02:53.007 --> 00:02:56.425
